The first independent differential found 74 canonical/generated disagreements among 36,302 string cases. Importantly, the generated program had zero disagreements with the literal prompt oracle; the mounted canonical is the outlier on dates such as `01-30-2000` because its unparenthesized conditions reject day 30 or 31 globally, while it also accepts stripped/unpadded forms. I’ll keep that intent-versus-canonical limitation separate from the K proof’s soundness as I rebuild the definitions now.
The supplied-semantics integrity boundary and source/translator checks passed. The independent fidelity test exposed canonical/generated divergences that must be judged at intent adequacy, while the generated implementation matched the literal prompt oracle over the preserved sample.
